{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "kanban-specify-bounded-lossless-review-paging-as-a-host-projection-1793018631769", :event/time "2026-10-26T12:43:51.769Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "specify-bounded-lossless-review-paging-as-a-host-projection", :dependency [], :parent nil, :card-type "task", :type "task-created", :write-id "1793018631767-0.dy3lnpucpue0pj1apsc", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Specify bounded lossless review paging as a host projection", :source-path "/home/err/.local/share/codex-work/axxium-sso/muse-review-paging-plan/docs/agile/kanban/specify-bounded-lossless-review-paging-as-a-host-projection.md", :status "incoming", :body "## Context\n\nThe shared Axxium login release is waiting on qualified native assessments, not merely builds. Protected ETA run [40264714320](https://github.com/open-hax/eta-mu/actions/runs/40264714320) timed out after 120 minutes having read and assessed 63 of 146 lossless input pages; publication was skipped. This is failed diagnostic evidence, not an accepted judgment. Its Knoxx head is now stale and must not be reused.\n\nThe immutable compatibility implementation [diff-chunks at c1369c2](https://github.com/riatzukiza/muse/blob/c1369c223cf3c57e3e31934a6d746bfcdfe73f5a/src/cljs/eta_mu/domain/review.cljc#L78) fixes each page at 8,192 UTF-16 units and at most 128 lines. It preserves surrogate pairs and exact text concatenation. The 1,191,002-byte assessment envelope contains complete native context, source postimages, changed files, preimages and canonical protocol. No component is declared dispensable. A simple observed-rate extrapolation is about 278 minutes, beyond the accepted 180-minute maximum; this estimate is not a benchmark or a completion guarantee.\n\nCanonical body-intent purpose planning is [riatzukiza/.agents#47](https://github.com/riatzukiza/.agents/pull/47), consumed by Foresight NRI-2 card `29b50a33-6ecf-4955-85c5-f8ec72c8ac22`. That purpose and protected publisher remain separate from this proposal.\n\n## Outcome\n\nDescribe and independently review a bounded, lossless page-delivery projection that reduces host/model round trips while preserving every byte of source/context and every existing assessment obligation. Obtain an explicit ownership disposition before implementation.\n\n## Scope and ownership\n\n- Muse may own target linking, codecs and emitted host artifacts. Its compatibility repository is not authority for actor, session, policy, workflow or evidence semantics. A file's current location is implementation lineage, not ownership permission.\n- Propose only a pure representation primitive and a trusted host-profile seam. Keep selection of the complete input, review stages, assessment decisions, approval/settlement laws and publication authority with their existing owners. Do not migrate those domains into Muse to deliver this change.\n- Owning review must decide whether this primitive belongs in Muse's target projection or must be consumed from an eta-mu/Sol/shared shape owner. If ownership is rejected or ambiguous, stop implementation and update this plan with the owning resource and consumption seam; do not duplicate the primitive.\n- Candidate transport limits are a closed set of 8,192, 16,384 and 32,768 UTF-16 units per page, retaining the current 128-line bound. The current limit remains the default. Review these values as resource limits, not claims that a model can process them within a deadline.\n- Only an immutable, operator-selected host/purpose profile may select a supported limit before session creation. The model and untrusted review text cannot select or change it. Do not introduce a caller-controlled environment override or silent fallback.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNo HTML/review-intent parser, classification-to-approval conversion, new assessor/provider credentials, semantic review-policy engine, board implementation, automatic retry, budget increase, source truncation, permission widening, deployment, account linking or federation cutover. This card does not implement NRI-2, NRI-3 or the typed Kimi publisher.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Independent planning review settles the transport primitive's owner and named consumption seam before code or profile changes.\n- [ ] Missing configuration preserves the current page text, IDs and start/end coordinates exactly. Invalid explicit values refuse before execution; they do not silently become a default.\n- [ ] Every supported partition concatenates to the exact original input, preserves Unicode surrogate pairs, CRLF/LF and trailing text, respects both bounds, and neither duplicates nor omits content.\n- [ ] Page IDs/coordinates and delivered/assessed coverage are derived from the selected immutable profile and input. Missing, stale, duplicated or partially assessed pages cannot satisfy existing submission requirements. A changed input/profile requires a fresh session and proof.\n- [ ] Trusted artifact/profile provenance and the selected transport limits are inspectable. A model request cannot alter them. Old consumers continue to use the default until a separate, reviewed protected consumer adopts an option.\n- [ ] Meaningful red/green tests include unchanged-default parity, adversarial long/Unicode inputs, invalid limits, reconstruction, and existing incomplete-coverage refusal; no second implementation of approval or settlement law is added.\n- [ ] Local tests/builds are preparation only. Protected ETA adoption, an accepted complete native invocation within its bound, independent App publication/readback and revocation qualification remain explicit downstream obligations.\n\n## Verification\n\nPlanning checks: review the immutable source and failure metadata, verify native Rheos creation/readback and unchanged initial status, and check the diff. Do not rerun the failed assessment to validate this document. Implementation later must run the owning repository's zero-warning Clojure and artifact gates and preserve prior page/coverage behavior under the default profile.\n\nA separate protected ETA consumer must bind the reviewed emitter/source/profile and stable current target, preserve all required input and permissions, then demonstrate complete accepted execution within the existing 60–180-minute model-step envelope and publisher headroom. It must retain real failed outcomes and refuse edited/replayed or uncertain publication. Larger pages are a feasibility candidate, not acceptance evidence.\n\n## Risks\n\nA larger response can increase inference latency or exceed a model's practical context. An input cap can silently become truncation unless completeness remains independently checked. Repartitioning can invalidate coverage evidence, hashes and cache keys. Profile selection exposed to a model creates a confused authority boundary. Compatibility-file ownership may require a different upstream home. All of these remain blockers until independently reviewed and verified; no old trace supplies a new verdict."}, :causal/root "83587310-2836-4e21-a2a1-39b41dbc335e"}
{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "kanban-d1d94066-abb7-4439-af0e-cfdd8df4f337-1793026677516", :event/time "2026-10-26T14:57:57.516Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "d1d94066-abb7-4439-af0e-cfdd8df4f337", :dependency [], :parent nil, :card-type "task", :type "task-created", :write-id "1793026677514-0.8ivois15bufgpzw68kk", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Plan bounded lossless review delivery and ownership", :source-path "/home/err/.local/share/codex-work/axxium-sso/muse-review-paging-plan/docs/agile/kanban/plan-bounded-lossless-review-delivery-and-ownership-8df4f337.md", :status "incoming", :body "## Context\n\nProtected ETA run [40264714320](https://github.com/open-hax/eta-mu/actions/runs/40264714320) timed out after 120 minutes with 63 of 146 pages assessed and publication skipped. This is failed diagnostic evidence on a now-stale Knoxx target, not a judgment.\n\nThe pinned [Muse compatibility emitter c1369c2](https://github.com/riatzukiza/muse/blob/c1369c223cf3c57e3e31934a6d746bfcdfe73f5a/src/cljs/eta_mu/domain/review.cljc#L78) fixes pages at 8,192 UTF-16 units and 128 lines. The complete original manifest-bound input is 1,191,389 UTF-8 bytes and 1,191,002 UTF-16 units. Earlier notes called the latter bytes; this is a unit correction, not an input change.\n\nSee [the full-input feasibility report](../../review-paging-feasibility.md): isolated evaluation of the pinned primitive with only its numeric page cap varied gives 146, 73 and 37 pages at 8,192, 16,384 and 32,768 units. Every candidate retains the 128-line bound and reconstructs the original SHA-256. No runtime/model deadline or coverage acceptance follows from page count.\n\n## Outcome\n\nComplete an independently reviewed ownership and delivery plan. This card ends with accepted planning artifacts, not implementation, a model judgment or deployment.\n\n## Scope and ownership\n\n- Establish the transport primitive owner and named consumption seam. Muse may project target artifacts and codecs, but cannot acquire actor, session, workflow, review-policy, evidence or publication authority from a compatibility file's location.\n- Specify unchanged default behavior and a closed candidate cap set with trusted immutable operator-profile selection before session creation. Preserve complete input, Unicode, coordinates and coverage requirements in the proposed implementation contract.\n- Record a stop/reconsider decision if complete-input page-count reduction is absent or an owning review rejects the seam. Do not patch a compatibility copy while ownership is ambiguous.\n- This is a local root planning card with no local parent/dependency. The external Foresight NRI-2 card `29b50a33-6ecf-4955-85c5-f8ec72c8ac22` and [.agents#47](https://github.com/riatzukiza/.agents/pull/47) are consumer/purpose references, not invented local graph links.\n- Separately estimated follow-ups: implementation `7ee34a27-324a-4201-b026-f8d9ae6691ee` (5 points) depends on this card; protected-consumer qualification `6118415f-632c-49e2-8970-cd614c0b8628` (8 points) depends on implementation. Estimates are provisional until planning review accepts them.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNo executable review-tool/profile changes, parser, classifier-to-approval conversion, new credentials, model retry, permission widening, larger timeout, input truncation, account link, deployment or federation cutover. This card does not implement NRI-2/NRI-3 or the typed Kimi publisher.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Independent review accepts the primitive's owner and exact consumption seam, or records refusal and an explicitly blocked handoff; ambiguous ownership never authorizes code.\n- [ ] The report binds the immutable source and complete motivating input, records page counts and binding bounds for every candidate, proves reconstruction and unchanged-default parity, and states the go/stop rationale without predicting accepted model completion.\n- [ ] The proposed implementation contract specifies default parity, invalid-value refusal, surrogate/CRLF/trailing-text preservation, fresh sessions for changed input/profile, trusted provenance and unchanged incomplete-coverage refusal.\n- [ ] Separate implementation and protected-consumer qualification cards have explicit UUID dependencies, outcome boundaries, estimates, non-goals and verification obligations.\n- [ ] Native Rheos readback confirms this card and dependency graph; immutable creation/supersession history is retained; all planning findings are settled before a lawful ready transition.\n\n## Verification\n\nRead-only full-input partition measurement and native Rheos creation/readback are planning evidence. Review this diff and immutable source/failure metadata. Do not rerun the failed model invocation or call document approval an executable qualification.\n\n## Risks\n\nLarger responses may increase latency/context pressure. The motivating input is stale for admission. A character cap cannot help line-limited pages; this particular full input is character-limited, but future inputs may differ. Profile and ownership choices remain pending independent review. Completing this plan does not complete either follow-up."}, :causal/root "fd41041e-637a-430c-b529-adccad10a953"}
